# uv (not used by this project; pip + requirements.lock is the source of truth)
uv.lock

# Local runbook selection (training side). The SERVING artifacts under
# src/daintree_assistant_server/runbooks/local/artifacts/ ship in the image (see below).
# Everything here is the machinery that produced them and
# is reproducible from `training/`, so it stays out of the repo.
# NOTE: git has no trailing-comment syntax — a "path  # why" line makes the
# comment part of the pattern and silently matches nothing. Keep these bare.
# HuggingFace hub / datasets cache:
training/.cache/
# Trainer checkpoints + tensorboard logs:
training/runs/
# Fine-tuned torch checkpoints, pre-ONNX-export:
training/models/
# Training stdout captures:
training/logs/
# Per-run result JSONs and the report page. Chunky, regenerable, and the numbers
# that matter are transcribed into training/EXPERIMENTS.md — which is the record.
# The report is published as a claude.ai artifact, not carried in the repo.
training/results/
# NOT ignored, and each for its own reason — the corpus is three planes:
#   training/journals/  RAW. What a generating agent actually returned. Committed
#                       BECAUSE it is not reconstructible: the generator is a
#                       nondeterministic paid model, so a discarded journal is a
#                       row that can never be traced to a prompt again. These used
#                       to be ignored, which left the generated artifact as the
#                       only evidence and made "regenerate" mean "append".
#   training/corpus/    CURATED. Hand-edited YAML; the source of truth.
#   training/data/      COMPILED. selection.jsonl + corpus-lock.json, both produced
#                       by training.compile_corpus and gated in CI against the
#                       curated plane. Committed as the record of what the shipped
#                       weights were trained on — ~3 MB, well under anything that
#                       would justify LFS or DVC.

# Local runbook selection (serving side). The model files (the ONNX graphs, the tokenizer
# vocabularies and vectors.npz) are NOT in Git: they live in the bucket selector.lock names,
# addressed by hash, and `training/fetch_selector.sh` puts them here. What stays tracked is
# the small text beside them (meta.json, labels.json, tokenizer_config.json, ...).
# Only the served precision ships: the int8 ranking encoder and the fp32 RETRIEVER. The fp32
# ranking graph exists only so the exporter can measure what quantisation costs, is never
# stored, and is ignored with the rest.
#
# vectors.npz is stored with the model, not rebuilt: every row is keyed by the digest of the
# document it was built from, so serving re-embeds exactly what moved and reuses the rest;
# shipping it just means the first turn after a deploy does not pay for embedding a catalog
# that usually has not changed.
src/daintree_assistant_server/runbooks/local/artifacts/**/*.onnx
src/daintree_assistant_server/runbooks/local/artifacts/**/*.npz
src/daintree_assistant_server/runbooks/local/artifacts/**/tokenizer.json
# vocab.txt is a ~30k-line side-file the exporter emits beside tokenizer.json,
# which is self-contained and is what `_tokenizer` actually loads
# (Tokenizer.from_file). Verified by removing both from a checkout: the token ids
# come out identical.
# NOTE the scope. This is deliberately NOT widened back over the rest of the
# tokenizer directory: special_tokens_map.json is 695 bytes and belongs to a
# HuggingFace tokenizer dir, and an artifact that ships minus files its own
# exporter wrote is a trap for whoever debugs it next. This glob was written for
# the old classifier/ layout and silently swallowed the selector/ tokenizers when
# that landed, which cost real time to rule out.
src/daintree_assistant_server/runbooks/local/artifacts/**/vocab.txt
# Superseded artifact layouts. The single fixed-head classifier is torn out (this
# branch); the retrieve-then-rerank pipeline before it was measured and abandoned
# (training/EXPERIMENTS.md). Kept as ignores so a stale local export cannot land.
src/daintree_assistant_server/runbooks/local/artifacts/classifier/
src/daintree_assistant_server/runbooks/local/artifacts/index/
src/daintree_assistant_server/runbooks/local/artifacts/bi_encoder/
src/daintree_assistant_server/runbooks/local/artifacts/reranker/
src/daintree_assistant_server/runbooks/local/artifacts/docs_head.npz

# Local training traces (TRACE_SINK=filesystem). These may contain FULL user
# content — messages, tool arguments, terminal output. Never commit them, and
# never include them in a diagnostic bundle or a copytree.
.tmp/traces/

# The pre-rename package path. `skills/` -> `runbooks/` moved every TRACKED file
# out via `git mv`; it never touches the untracked fp32 export intermediates
# (`model.onnx`, `vocab.txt` — the shipped artifact is the int8 ranker, the fp32
# retriever and `tokenizer.json` under runbooks/) that a local export run had already dropped
# there. Nothing loads them and nothing ever should: nothing under the old
# package path is a real source location any more, so the whole directory is
# ignored rather than pattern-matched file by file, which is what let these
# resurface in every git client's changed-files view despite never having been
# committed — untracked status is re-derived from scratch on every refresh, so
# a file nothing ignores looks "new" forever, not just once.
src/daintree_assistant_server/skills/
